  "notes": "Composed of {発|はつ} (emit, discharge) + {射|しゃ} (shoot). Covers both firing weapons and launching rockets or missiles.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {銃|じゅう}を{発射|はっしゃ}する: to fire a gun\n- ロケットを{発射|はっしゃ}する: to launch a rocket\n- ミサイルを{発射|はっしゃ}する: to launch a missile\n- {発射|はっしゃ}{台|だい}: launch pad\n- {発射|はっしゃ}{音|おん}: firing sound\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {撃|う}つ: to shoot — more general and everyday; used for shooting guns, hitting targets\n- {打|う}ち{上|あ}げる: to launch, to set off — used for rockets and fireworks; emphasizes the upward motion\n- {発進|はっしん}する: to set off, depart — for vehicles or aircraft beginning movement, not projectiles",
